From: OE-Alliance <build@oe-alliance.org>
Subject: [PATCH] STB: distinguish media audio timestamps from GUI timing

The HiSi hardware audio clock path must only follow video for media-timed
packets. Keep GUI/keepalive audio independent of the video decoder.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STB hardware integration]

--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkSTB.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Sinks/AESinkSTB.cpp
@@ -285,6 +285,7 @@ unsigned int CAESinkSTB::AddPackets(uint8_t** data,
   packet.size = static_cast<size_t>(frames) * m_format.m_frameSize;
   packet.pts_90k = m_nextPts90k;
   packet.duration_90k = duration90k;
+  packet.flags = m_hasMediaTimestamp ? STBP_AUDIO_PACKET_MEDIA_PTS : 0;
   result = stbp_audio_queue_packet(m_device, &packet);
   if (result == STBP_AGAIN)
     return 0;
